// Boxes that float over others, as Clay has them: from a point of the
// box under to a point of their own, as big as that box or a share of it,
// a layer above it or in one they ask for; and the pointer, which is over
// the boxes of the topmost layer it is in, unless they let it through.
// RUN: %ent run -I %S/../../examples %S/Inputs/layout_floats.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s

// The badge has its middle on the panel's bottom right corner, 3 to the
// right. The veil is as big as the window, in the layer it asked for. The
// menu is half as wide as the panel and a quarter as high, under its
// bottom left corner, and what is in it fills it. The pointer is on the
// panel: over it and the window, the veil letting it through.
// CHECK:      1: root 0.0 0.0 400.0 300.0 layer 0 pointer 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: panel 20.0 20.0 200.0 100.0 layer 0 pointer 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: item 22.0 122.0 96.0 21.0 layer 1 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: badge 213.0 115.0 20.0 10.0 layer 1 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: veil 0.0 0.0 400.0 300.0 layer 5 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: menu 20.0 120.0 100.0 25.0 layer 1 pointer 0
// On the menu: over it and what is in it, and no more over the window
// under them.
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: root 0.0 0.0 400.0 300.0 layer 0 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: panel 20.0 20.0 200.0 100.0 layer 0 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: item 22.0 122.0 96.0 21.0 layer 1 pointer 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: badge 213.0 115.0 20.0 10.0 layer 1 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: veil 0.0 0.0 400.0 300.0 layer 5 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: menu 20.0 120.0 100.0 25.0 layer 1 pointer 1
// Just outside the menu, which is 4 bigger for the pointer than its box,
// and down.
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: root 0.0 0.0 400.0 300.0 layer 0 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: panel 20.0 20.0 200.0 100.0 layer 0 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: item 22.0 122.0 96.0 21.0 layer 1 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: badge 213.0 115.0 20.0 10.0 layer 1 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: veil 0.0 0.0 400.0 300.0 layer 5 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: menu 20.0 120.0 100.0 25.0 layer 1 pointer 2
// The panel is narrower: what floats over it is where and as big as it
// says now, in the same frame.
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: root 0.0 0.0 400.0 300.0 layer 0 pointer 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: panel 20.0 20.0 100.0 100.0 layer 0 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: item 22.0 122.0 46.0 21.0 layer 1 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: badge 113.0 115.0 20.0 10.0 layer 1 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: veil 0.0 0.0 400.0 300.0 layer 5 pointer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: menu 20.0 120.0 50.0 25.0 layer 1 pointer 0
